Relevant columns and how they can help  

• event_date : to keep only rows from 20180801‑20180930  
• event_name : to spot installs (first_open) and un‑installs (app_remove)  
• event_timestamp : to measure the “7‑day” window (micro‑seconds since epoch)  
• user_pseudo_id : stable anonymous user id – the unit we count  
• event_params : some GA events keep extra attributes here, but for this exercise we only need to know which rows are “app_remove” or “first_open”

Typical conditions you will add  

• event_date BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'  
• event_name IN ('first_open','app_remove')  
• TIMESTAMP_MICROS(app_remove_ts) <= TIMESTAMP_MICROS(first_open_ts)+INTERVAL 7 DAY   ( to find uninstalls ≤7‑days )  

Below are 10 exploratory → incremental → final BigQuery SQL snippets (each returns ≤20 rows just to inspect; remove the LIMIT when you want the full result).  
All table names are in dataset firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282 and are daily‑partitioned, so we read them with the wildcard events_2018* and then filter on event_date.

```sql
-- 1. Quick look at the distinct event names on 1‑Aug‑2018
SELECT DISTINCT event_name
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_20180801`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Count the top‑20 events during Aug‑Sep 2018
SELECT event_name, COUNT(*) AS hits
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_2018*`
WHERE event_date BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
GROUP BY event_name
ORDER BY hits DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Show a few rows of the uninstall event to verify it is called “app_remove”
SELECT event_date, event_timestamp, user_pseudo_id, event_params
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_2018*`
WHERE event_name = 'app_remove'
  AND event_date BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Take a glimpse of installations (first_open) in the period
SELECT event_date, user_pseudo_id, event_timestamp
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_2018*`
WHERE event_name = 'first_open'
  AND event_date BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. One first_open per user (their first one in Aug‑Sep)
SELECT user_pseudo_id,
       MIN(event_timestamp) AS first_open_ts
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_2018*`
WHERE event_name = 'first_open'
  AND event_date BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. For the same users, look at their earliest uninstall during the window
SELECT user_pseudo_id,
       MIN(event_timestamp) AS uninstall_ts
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_2018*`
WHERE event_name = 'app_remove'
  AND event_date BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Join installs & uninstalls, keep flag if uninstalled ≤7 days
WITH installs AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id,
         MIN(event_timestamp) AS first_open_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_2018*`
  WHERE event_name = 'first_open'
    AND event_date BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
),
uninstalls AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id,
         MIN(event_timestamp) AS uninstall_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_2018*`
  WHERE event_name = 'app_remove'
    AND event_date BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
)
SELECT i.user_pseudo_id,
       i.first_open_ts,
       u.uninstall_ts,
       u.uninstall_ts IS NOT NULL 
         AND u.uninstall_ts <= i.first_open_ts + 7*24*60*60*1000000 AS uninstalled_within_7d
FROM installs i
LEFT JOIN uninstalls u
USING (user_pseudo_id)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Calculate counts of each category (≤7d, >7d, never)
WITH installs AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id,
         MIN(event_timestamp) AS first_open_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_2018*`
  WHERE event_name = 'first_open'
    AND event_date BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
),
uninstalls AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id,
         MIN(event_timestamp) AS uninstall_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_2018*`
  WHERE event_name = 'app_remove'
    AND event_date BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
)
SELECT
  COUNT(*) AS installs,
  SUM(CASE
        WHEN u.uninstall_ts IS NULL THEN 1           -- never uninstalled
        WHEN u.uninstall_ts > i.first_open_ts + 7*24*60*60*1000000 THEN 1 -- >7d
        ELSE 0
      END) AS kept_≥7d_or_never,
  SUM(CASE
        WHEN u.uninstall_ts IS NOT NULL
         AND u.uninstall_ts <= i.first_open_ts + 7*24*60*60*1000000 THEN 1
        ELSE 0
      END) AS uninstalled_≤7d
FROM installs i
LEFT JOIN uninstalls u
USING (user_pseudo_id)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Same as previous but compute the percentage
WITH installs AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id,
         MIN(event_timestamp) AS first_open_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_2018*`
  WHERE event_name = 'first_open'
    AND event_date BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
),
uninstalls AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id,
         MIN(event_timestamp) AS uninstall_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_2018*`
  WHERE event_name = 'app_remove'
    AND event_date BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
)
SELECT
  COUNT(*) AS total_installs,
  SUM(CASE
        WHEN u.uninstall_ts IS NULL
          OR u.uninstall_ts > i.first_open_ts + 7*24*60*60*1000000
      THEN 1
      ELSE 0
      END)                                    AS kept_users,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(
      SUM(CASE
            WHEN u.uninstall_ts IS NULL
              OR u.uninstall_ts > i.first_open_ts + 7*24*60*60*1000000
          THEN 1
          ELSE 0
          END),
      COUNT(*)
  ) AS pct_kept
FROM installs i
LEFT JOIN uninstalls u
USING (user_pseudo_id)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final query (remove the LIMIT when you need the real value)
--     percentage of users who did NOT uninstall within 7 days
WITH installs AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id,
         MIN(event_timestamp) AS first_open_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_2018*`
  WHERE event_name = 'first_open'
    AND event_date BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
),
uninstalls AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id,
         MIN(event_timestamp) AS uninstall_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_2018*`
  WHERE event_name = 'app_remove'
    AND event_date BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
)
SELECT
  ROUND(100 * SAFE_DIVIDE(
      SUM(CASE
            WHEN u.uninstall_ts IS NULL
              OR u.uninstall_ts > i.first_open_ts + 7*24*60*60*1000000
          THEN 1 ELSE 0 END),
      COUNT(*)),2) AS pct_of_users_keep_app_≥7d_or_never
FROM installs i
LEFT JOIN uninstalls u
USING (user_pseudo_id)
LIMIT 20;
```

Run query 10 without the final `LIMIT` to obtain the actual percentage of August–September‑2018 installers who either never uninstalled or did so only after the 7‑day mark.
